WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.868
-Welcome, everybody.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:05.200
Thank you for being here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.434 --> 00:00:09.434
Well, guys, it seems like

00:00:09.434 --> 00:00:11.400
there's so much going on
right now.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:14.200
Supreme Court justice Stephen
Breyer is stepping down.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:17.601
Everyone's talking about
"Encanto."

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:22.100
A winter hurricane might be
headed for the East Coast.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:25.968
And Pizza Hut just released
its spiciest pizza ever.

00:00:25.968 --> 00:00:28.133
Let's just jump in
and cover it all at once.

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:30.400
It's time for a "News Smash."

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:32.234 --> 00:00:34.968
♪♪

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:36.767
First up, Justice Breyer.

00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:39.901
He's retiring after nearly
30 years on the Supreme Court.

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:42.701
Democrats are already talking
about who should replace him.

00:00:42.701 --> 00:00:44.734
But you know who
they're not talking about?

00:00:44.734 --> 00:00:46.868
Bruno.

00:00:46.868 --> 00:00:48.767
"Encanto" is huge right now.

00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:51.434
It's got an amazing soundtrack
by Lin-Manuel Miranda,

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:52.834
and two of the songs
are currently

00:00:52.834 --> 00:00:54.534
in the Billboard Top 10.

00:00:54.534 --> 00:00:56.501
The music is rocking everyone
like a...

00:00:56.501 --> 00:00:58.334
hurricane.

00:00:58.334 --> 00:01:01.234
That's right. A bomb cyclone
with the power of a hurricane

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:03.100
is headed for the Northeast.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:04.434
And if you want to experience

00:01:04.434 --> 00:01:06.901
your own personal bomb cyclone,
why not try...

00:01:06.901 --> 00:01:09.901
Pizza Hut's new
Spicy Lover's Pizza?

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:11.868
It's their spiciest pizza ever.

00:01:11.868 --> 00:01:14.234
With red jalapeños
and chili peppers.

00:01:14.234 --> 00:01:16.100
It will mess you up so bad,
you'll have to...

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:18.400
retire.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:20.868
Whoever fills Breyer's seat
will be stuck in that role

00:01:20.868 --> 00:01:22.534
for years to come.

00:01:22.534 --> 00:01:24.434
Speaking of things
getting stuck for years,

00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:25.934
the "Encanto" soundtrack.

00:01:25.934 --> 00:01:29.033
We're gonna be singing
these songs for a long time.

00:01:29.033 --> 00:01:30.334
It's basically the new...

00:01:30.334 --> 00:01:31.968
"Frozen."

00:01:31.968 --> 00:01:35.467
To prepare, people are stocking
up on water and toilet paper,

00:01:35.467 --> 00:01:38.601
but not because of the storm,
because they just tried...

00:01:38.601 --> 00:01:41.667
Pizza Hut's new
Spicy Lover's Pizza.

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:44.234
In conclusion, time to go...

00:01:44.234 --> 00:01:45.834
let it snow...

00:01:45.834 --> 00:01:47.467
get that dough...

00:01:47.467 --> 00:01:50.133
♪ We don't talk about Bruno,
no, no, no ♪

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:52.400
This has been a "News Smash."

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:58.067 --> 00:01:59.367
Thank you.

00:01:59.367 --> 00:02:01.267
Well, as I mentioned,
this weekend,

00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:04.000
a giant winter storm is heading
for the East Coast.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.167
But I saw this one tweet
from NBC News

00:02:06.167 --> 00:02:08.234
that wasn't super-helpful.

00:02:08.234 --> 00:02:10.067
It said New York City could see

00:02:10.067 --> 00:02:13.901
between 2 inches and 20 inches
of snow this weekend.

00:02:13.901 --> 00:02:16.067
-[ Laughter ]
-Oh, thanks a lot.

00:02:16.067 --> 00:02:17.300
-Yeah, now I know.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:19.400
-Pretty big range right there.
I don't know --

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:21.934
Who's making these predictions?
The CDC?

00:02:21.934 --> 00:02:23.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.934 --> 00:02:27.501
"Six feet, three feet,
ten days, five days.

00:02:27.501 --> 00:02:29.567
We don't know. We don't know."

00:02:29.567 --> 00:02:31.100
Yeah, so you'll either be
going to work

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.667
or you'll be buried
inside your house,

00:02:32.667 --> 00:02:34.334
so get ready.

00:02:34.334 --> 00:02:35.834
Some business news.

00:02:35.834 --> 00:02:39.133
Bud Light just announced they're
releasing Bud Light Next,

00:02:39.133 --> 00:02:43.834
a zero-carb beer that they spent
nearly ten years trying to make.

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:45.434
Ten years.

00:02:45.434 --> 00:02:47.834
Wow. Somehow it took a few
months for the Pfizer vaccine,

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:52.367
but ten years
for Bud Light Next.

00:02:52.367 --> 00:02:54.000
Here's some good news.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.000
Delta Airlines
will soon bring back

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.501
hot meal service on its flights.

00:02:58.501 --> 00:03:00.901
Meanwhile, Spirit is like,
"That's why we put the engine

00:03:00.901 --> 00:03:05.133
in the cabin, so people can
heat up whatever they want."

00:03:05.133 --> 00:03:08.968
Hey, guys, I read that Elon Musk
took his kids to Walmart

00:03:08.968 --> 00:03:10.601
so they could see the pandemic

00:03:10.601 --> 00:03:13.767
toilet-paper shortage
firsthand.

00:03:13.767 --> 00:03:16.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.601 --> 00:03:18.901
His kids were like,
"This is crazy, Dad!

00:03:18.901 --> 00:03:21.701
Why don't they just use
$100 bills like we do?"

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:25.634
"That's right.
Let's go home now."

00:03:25.634 --> 00:03:28.734
Finally, I heard,
because of staff shortages,

00:03:28.734 --> 00:03:31.100
the governor of New Mexico
had to fill in

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:34.868
as a substitute teacher
at an elementary school.

00:03:34.868 --> 00:03:36.834
Yeah, it's pretty effective
when the teacher says,

00:03:36.834 --> 00:03:39.334
"Behave, or I'm raising your
parents' property taxes."

00:03:39.334 --> 00:03:40.634
We have a great show.

